    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūrĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m.
		curia. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The priest of a curia</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, §
			46</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maximus,</span>”
				<i>he who presided over all the curiæ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 8, 1</span></i>
			; cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 126, 17</span></i>
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Post-Aug., <i>a crier, herald</i>, =
			praeco, Mart. l<i><span class="en">ib. 2 praef.</span></i>; Treb. Gall.
		12.</div>
